{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.TopologicalMass.cat_eigenspace_decomposition","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.TopologicalMass.cat_eigenspace_decomposition","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.TopologicalMass.not_cat_eigenspace_decomposition_of_free_data","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.TopologicalMass.not_cat_eigenspace_decomposition_of_free_data","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/TopologicalMass/cat_eigenspace_decomposition.lean#L116-L122","doc":"**The decomposition is refutable at freely-chosen data**, which is why it\nis named rather than carried as a `sorry`.\n\nWith every function constantly zero and `m(ρ) = 1` it reads `1 = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.TopologicalMass.cat_eigenspace_decomposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.TopologicalMass.cat_eigenspace_decomposition","kind":"def","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/TopologicalMass/cat_eigenspace_decomposition.lean#L103-L114","doc":"**Orthogonal decomposition of the categorical mass**\n([`lem:topological-mass-cat-eigenspace`]), as a proposition over\ncaller-supplied data:\n\n`m(ρ) = ‖tr(τ̂_n(α))‖ + ‖tr(α − τ̂_n(α))‖`.\n\n**Named, not asserted.** Read the module docstring first: with `nrm` and `tr`\narbitrary functions this is not yet a statement about norms or traces, and\nthe norm-additivity that is the lemma's actual content is open. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:lem:topological-mass-cat-eigenspace","label":"lem:topological-mass-cat-eigenspace","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/topological-mass-cat-eigenspace.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.TopologicalMass.transient_antiInvariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.TopologicalMass.transient_antiInvariant","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/TopologicalMass/cat_eigenspace_decomposition.lean#L90-L101","doc":"**The transient component is anti-invariant** — the eigenspace content of\nthe lemma's name, derived.\n\nIf the descent map is additive on differences and involutive, then\n`τ̂(α − τ̂α) = −(α − τ̂α)`: the transient part lies in the `−1` eigenspace of\n`τ̂`. Sorry-free, and independent of any norm or pairing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.TopologicalMass.split_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.TopologicalMass.split_eq","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/TopologicalMass/cat_eigenspace_decomposition.lean#L79-L88","doc":"**The algebraic split is a tautology**, and is recorded as one.\n\n`α = τ̂(α) + (α − τ̂(α))` holds for every function `τ̂` whatever — no descent,\nno involution, no pairing. It is stated here because an earlier version of\nthis file presented exactly this identity, routed through a fictitious\n`intermediate_sum`, as the lemma's content. Naming it as trivial is what\nkeeps it from being mistaken for the claim again. ","signatureChunk":0}]}